          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.4,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are left with 2 tenths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.113,
            0.847,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To divide 2 Tenths into 4 equal parts, we have to regroup them as 20 Hundredths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.225,
            0.157,
            0.773,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.225,
                0.157,
                0.773,
                0.35
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.375,
            0.655,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "20 Hundredths ÷ 4 Each part gets 5 Hundredths."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.395,
            0.904,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.153,
                0.395,
                0.904,
                0.652
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.67,
            0.846,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, 1325 ÷ 4 = 0 Thousands + 3 Hundreds + 3 Tens + 1 Ones + 2 Tenths + 5 Hundredths. This we know is 331.25, thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.708,
            0.585,
            0.727
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_7.jpg",
          "content": "1325 \\div 4 = 331.25."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.733,
            0.75,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we verify this by finding an equivalent fraction for "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 3 2 5 } { 4 } ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.772,
            0.847,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To get an equivalent fraction such that the denominator is of the form 1, 10, 100, 1000, and so on, we can multiply the numerator and denominator by 25."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.365,
            0.834,
            0.632,
            0.873
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{1325 \\times 25}{4 \\times 25} = \\frac{33125}{100} = 331.25."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.934,
            0.187,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "80"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
